{
  "title": "A reject station: a colour sensor, a timer and a pusher",
  "about": "Start and Stop seal in the PLC's Running bit, which runs the belt motor M1 on its contactor (0.4 m/s). Good boxes are brown; red ones are rejects. The colour sensor B1 sees a red box 0.8 m before the pusher; the PLC times its trip with T1 (preset Delay) and then fires valve Y1, and the paddle sweeps the box into the chute. Reed switch B2 says the rod is out; if it is not out within 1 s the PLC raises an alarm and stops. Counter C1 counts boxes out of the end (PE2), C2 boxes into the chute (PE3). Reset clears the counts and the alarm.",
  "dt": 0.002,
  "inputs": {
    "start": {
      "button": "Start",
      "color": "green"
    },
    "stop": {
      "button": "Stop",
      "nc": 1,
      "color": "red"
    },
    "reset": {
      "button": "Reset alarm and counts",
      "color": "blue"
    },
    "delay": {
      "slider": "Travel delay (T1 preset)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 0.1,
      "value": 2.0,
      "unit": "s",
      "hidden": true
    },
    "out_time": {
      "slider": "Pusher out time (T2 preset)",
      "min": 0.05,
      "max": 1,
      "step": 0.05,
      "value": 0.2,
      "unit": "s",
      "hidden": true
    },
    "speed": {
      "slider": "Belt speed (gearing)",
      "min": 0.2,
      "max": 0.8,
      "step": 0.05,
      "value": 0.4,
      "unit": "m/s",
      "hidden": true
    }
  },
  "let": {
    "b2_ok": "1",
    "rod_out": "AND(cyl.ext, b2_ok)",
    "pushed": "IF(belt.rejects > was, 1, IF(plc.Push, pushed, 0))",
    "pushed_k": "IF(belt.rej1 > was1, 1, IF(belt.rejects > was, 0, pushed_k))",
    "was": "belt.rejects",
    "was1": "belt.rej1",
    "pe3": "AND(pushed, cyl.pos > 0.3)",
    "binned": "belt.rejects - pushed",
    "binned_red": "belt.rej1 - pushed * pushed_k",
    "z_out1": "IF(reset, belt.out1, z_out1)",
    "z_rej": "IF(reset, belt.rejects, z_rej)",
    "z_rej1": "IF(reset, belt.rej1, z_rej1)",
    "red_through": "belt.out1 - z_out1",
    "red_rejected": "belt.rej1 - z_rej1",
    "good_rejected": "belt.rejects - z_rej - red_rejected"
  },
  "blocks": {
    "plc": {
      "type": "plc",
      "src": "VAR Running, Seen, Push, Alarm : BOOL; Delay, OutTime : TIME;\n    E1 : R_TRIG; T1, T2, T3 : TON; C1, C2 : CTU; END_VAR\n(* Start and Stop seal in Running; a pusher alarm stops the belt *)\nRunning := (Start OR Running) AND Stop AND NOT Alarm;\nBelt := Running;\n(* B1 sees a red box (its rising edge): Seen holds until T1 is done *)\nE1(CLK := Colour);\nSeen := (E1.Q OR Seen) AND Running AND NOT T1.Q;\n(* T1: the box's travel time from B1 to the pusher *)\nT1(IN := Seen, PT := Delay);\nIF T1.Q THEN Push := TRUE; END_IF;\n(* the rod stays out for OutTime once B2 says it is out; *)\n(* not out within 1 s (no air, stuck): alarm, and stop *)\nT2(IN := Push AND PushOut, PT := OutTime);\nT3(IN := Push AND NOT PushOut, PT := T#1s);\nIF T2.Q OR T3.Q THEN Push := FALSE; END_IF;\nIF T3.Q THEN Alarm := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF Reset THEN Alarm := FALSE; END_IF;\n(* the counts: a CTU adds 1 on each rising edge of CU *)\nC1(CU := EndEye, R := Reset, PV := 9999);\nC2(CU := Chute, R := Reset, PV := 9999);",
      "inputs": {
        "Start": "start",
        "Stop": "stop",
        "Reset": "reset",
        "Colour": "b1.on",
        "PushOut": "rod_out",
        "EndEye": "pe2.on",
        "Chute": "pe3",
        "Delay": "delay * 1000",
        "OutTime": "out_time * 1000"
      },
      "outputs": [
        "Belt",
        "Push",
        "Alarm"
      ]
    },
    "cyl": {
      "type": "cylinder",
      "extend": "plc.Push",
      "stroke": 0.35,
      "speed": 1.0,
      "back": 1.0
    },
    "m1": {
      "type": "motor",
      "f": 50,
      "on": "plc.Belt",
      "kw": 0.37,
      "rpm": 1370,
      "J": 0.003,
      "load": "0.4 + 0.1 * belt.n"
    },
    "belt": {
      "type": "conveyor",
      "rpm": "m1.n",
      "ratio": "1460 * PI() * 0.1 / 60 / speed",
      "dia": 0.1,
      "length": 2.8,
      "every": "0.6 / speed",
      "size": 0.2,
      "pattern": [
        0,
        0,
        1,
        0,
        0,
        1,
        0,
        0,
        0,
        1
      ],
      "eject": "AND(plc.Push, cyl.pos > 0.12)",
      "eject_at": 1.6,
      "preload": [
        1.9,
        1.3,
        0.7,
        0.1
      ]
    },
    "b1": {
      "type": "eye",
      "belt": "belt",
      "at": 0.8,
      "kind": 1
    },
    "pe2": {
      "type": "eye",
      "belt": "belt",
      "at": 2.6
    }
  },
  "faults": {
    "delay-short": {
      "label": "T1's preset (the travel delay) is too short",
      "why": "B1's lamp lights for each red box and T1 starts, but the pusher fires after 1 s, when the box has only gone 0.4 m of its 0.8 m: the paddle sweeps the empty belt in front of it and the red box rides on and off the end. Rejected (C2) stays at 0 and Red let through climbs. T1 ET stops at 1.00 s; the PLC's Delay tag says 1000 ms. The preset should be the travel time: 0.8 m ÷ 0.4 m/s = 2 s.",
      "set": {
        "delay": 1.0
      }
    },
    "delay-long": {
      "label": "T1's preset (the travel delay) is too long",
      "why": "B1 sees each red box and the pusher fires, but 3.5 s later: the red box has gone past and the paddle knocks off the good box behind it. Rejected (C2) still goes up once for each red box, so the count looks right, but Red let through and Good thrown away both climb. T1 ET runs to 3.50 s; it should stop at the travel time, 0.8 m ÷ 0.4 m/s = 2 s.",
      "set": {
        "delay": 3.5
      }
    },
    "colour-dead": {
      "label": "The colour sensor B1 is dead: it never sees a red box",
      "why": "B1's lamp never lights as a red box passes under it, so Seen is never set, T1 never starts (its ET stays at 0) and the pusher never moves: Rejected stays at 0 and every red box goes off the end. Check B1's supply and its LED, its signal wire to the PLC, and that its lens is clean and taught the right colour.",
      "set": {
        "b1.stuck": 0
      }
    },
    "no-air": {
      "label": "No air to the pusher (the supply is off, or a hose is off)",
      "why": "T1 times out and the PLC drives Y1 (its lamp lights) but the rod never moves, so B2 never says it is out. After 1 s T3 raises the alarm: the red light comes on, Y1 drops and the belt stops, with the red box just past the pusher. The PLC did its part; the valve has nothing to push with. Check the air pressure gauge, the isolating valve and the hoses, then Reset and Start.",
      "set": {
        "cyl.air": 0
      }
    },
    "b2-dead": {
      "label": "The pusher's reed switch B2 is dead (or has slipped along the barrel)",
      "why": "The pusher does fire and the red box goes into the chute (Rejected counts it), but B2's lamp never lights, so the PLC never learns the rod is out: it holds Y1 on until T3 raises the alarm after 1 s, then the belt stops. The rod moved, so it is not the air. A reed switch is clamped to the barrel and can slide or fail: check its LED with the rod held out, and its position.",
      "set": {
        "b2_ok": "0"
      }
    },
    "pe2-dead": {
      "label": "The count eye PE2 at the end is dead",
      "why": "Boxes leave the end, but PE2's lamp never lights and Good out (C1) stays at 0. Everything else is right: red boxes are still rejected and counted by C2. A counter can only count the edges it is given. Check PE2's supply and LED, its alignment with the reflector, and its wire.",
      "set": {
        "pe2.stuck": 0
      }
    }
  },
  "script": [
    {
      "at": 0.3,
      "say": "Four boxes wait on the belt: three good (brown) and one red, which must be rejected. Start is pressed…"
    },
    {
      "at": 1.0,
      "press": "start",
      "say": "Start: the PLC seals in Running and the belt motor's contactor pulls in. The belt runs at 0.4 m/s."
    },
    {
      "at": 1.3,
      "say": "The colour sensor B1 sees the red box. On that rising edge the PLC sets Seen, and timer T1 starts: 2 s, the time the box takes to travel the 0.8 m to the pusher."
    },
    {
      "at": 2.6,
      "say": "A good box breaks PE2's beam at the end. Counter C1 counts its rising edge: Good out 1."
    },
    {
      "at": 3.05,
      "say": "T1 is done: the red box is in front of the pusher. The PLC drives valve Y1 and the paddle sweeps the box off into the chute."
    },
    {
      "at": 3.6,
      "say": "Reed switch B2 saw the rod out; 0.2 s later (T2) the PLC lets it spring back. PE3 in the chute saw the box go by: C2 counts it, Rejected 1."
    },
    {
      "at": 5.5,
      "say": "The next red box reaches B1: Seen, T1 times its trip, and the pusher fires as it arrives. Every box out of the end is counted by C1."
    },
    {
      "at": 9.0,
      "press": "stop",
      "say": "Stop: Running drops and the belt stops. The counts stay until Reset."
    }
  ],
